    "mechanism": "Two read-only npu-smi 26.0.rc1 captures on the same anonymized machine, about 72 seconds apart, show the same mapping. The raw device name is Ascend910. NPU IDs 0 through 7 each occur in two table sections: one for Chip 0 and one for Chip 1. Their Phy-ID values span 0 through 15. For NPU 0 the pairs are Chip 0 / Phy-ID 0 / Bus-Id 0000:9D:00.0 and Chip 1 / Phy-ID 1 / Bus-Id 0000:9F:00.0; for NPU 7 they are Chip 0 / Phy-ID 14 / Bus-Id 0000:81:00.0 and Chip 1 / Phy-ID 15 / Bus-Id 0000:83:00.0. A board NPU ID, a within-board Chip ID and a global Phy-ID therefore identify different levels in this observed table. Resolve a requested (NPU ID, Chip ID) through the captured mapping before passing an identifier to an API that requires Phy-ID. The exact mapping is applicable only to the recorded machine, topology digest, device-name string and npu-smi version. A different or missing binding requires a fresh inventory. Both captures reported no running NPU processes; this fact does not demonstrate allocation anti-preemption, cross-host portability or performance. The raw name does not establish a 910C model designation.",
    "corrections": [
      "Corrected the raw-table structure: the NPU header repeats for each chip section; there is no separately observed board Bus-Id field.",
      "Retained four genuine applicability conditions; observation counts, parser identity and artifact hashes belong to evidence provenance.",
      "Two observations support only repeated mapping on one machine, without a lease, model-family or performance claim."
    ],
